formation Hiding Terminology)J118 102 :Mf0_12 sf-.105(\321 Results of an informal plenary meeting and additional proposals \321)A214 138 :M-.154(Collected by Birgit Pfitzmann)A94 181 :Mf0_10 sf1.017 .102(The common opinion among the participants of this workshop was that all the topics that)J94 193 :M.851 .085(Ross Anderson had chosen, such as steganography and fingerprinting, had indeed much in)J94 205 :M.704 .07(common, and that we all profited by learning about the treatment of these topics in usually)J94 217 :M.059 .006(quite different communities and from different points of view. To facilitate this, we decided to)J94 229 :M1.144 .114(agree on some common terminology in the final session of the workshop. I have tried to)J94 241 :M-.044(collect the results of this session, and added a few additional proposals.)A66 284 :Mf1_14 sf3.219 .322(The Terms Agreed Upon)J66 307 :Mf0_12 sf-.139(We decided that most of the applications have the following common core:)A:a36<3049883AB59CF039><3030304949498888883A3A3AB5B5B59C9C9CF0F0F0393939>fg null:b94 333 380 139 rC0<FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF><FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF>fg null:b54 484 :M-13 -12 :T%%DSIDICT:_cvuserdict /_cv known not {userdict /_cv 20 dict put}if_cv begin/bdf{bind def}bind def/isDeviceColor {/currentcolorspace where{pop currentcolorspace 0 get dup /DeviceGray eq exch dup /DeviceRGB eq exch /DeviceCMYK eq or or}{T}ifelse}bdf/setcmykcolor where{/setcmykcolor get /cvcmyk exch def}{/cvcmyk{1 sub 4 1 roll 3{3 index add neg dup 0 lt{pop 0}if 3 1 roll}repeat setrgbcolor pop}bdf }ifelse/stg{isDeviceColor {cf ca /cs load setscreen setgray}{pop}ifelse}bdf/strgb{isDeviceColor {cf ca /cs load setscreen setrgbcolor}{pop pop pop}ifelse}bdf/stcmyk{isDeviceColor {cf ca /cs load setscreen cvcmyk}{pop pop pop pop}ifelse}bdf/min1{dup 0 eq{pop 1}if}bdfcurrentscreen/cs exch def/ca exch def/cf exch defend13 12 :T0<FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF><FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF