> stands for \322text\323, \322message\323, \322image\323, or whatever)J66 552 :M-.046(seems appropriate. In the explanations, I use \322message\323.)A66 573 :M1(1.)A83 573 :M-.079(Embedded <datatype>. Something to be hidden in something else.)A66 594 :M1(2.)A83 594 :M.291 .029(Stego-<datatype>. The output of the hiding process; something that has the embedded)J83 609 :M-.065(message hidden in it.)A66 630 :M1(3.)A83 630 :M1.238 .124(Cover-<datatype>. An input with an \322original\323 form of the stegomessage. In some)J83 645 :M.065 .007(applications, such a covermessage is given from the outside, in others, it can be chosen)J83 660 :M.007 .001(during the hiding process. The latter is represented by the dashed extension to the inner)J83 675 :M.147 .015(hiding process.)J66 696 :M1(4.)A83 696 :M-.087(Stegokey or simply key. Additional secret data that may be needed in the hiding process.)A83 711 :M.107 .011(In particular, the same key \(or a related one\) is usually needed to extract the embedded)J83 726 :M-.049(message again.)Aendp%%Page: 2 2%%BeginPageSetupinitializepage(Birgit Pfitzmann; page: 2 of 4)setjob%%EndPageSetup-13 -12 :TgS 13 12 568 818 rC304 46 :Mf0_10 sf.417 .042<D1203220D1>J79 88 :Mf0_12 sf1.487 .149(There was no time to decide on names for further objects, but individual authors are)J79 103 :M1.427 .143(strongly encouraged to introduce additional or deviating terminology by extending or)J79 118 :M-.075(modifying the figure above.)A79 150 :Mf1_14 sf3.529 .353(A Few Additional Proposals)J79 173 :Mf0_12 sf-.085(I will venture to make a few more proposals, at least as a reference for other proposals:)A:a36<3049883AB59CF039><3030304949498888883A3A3AB5B5B59C9C9CF0F0F0393939>fg bk:b100 199 394 201 rC:e0 G473 151 :M%%DSIDICT:_cvuserdict /_cv known not {userdict /_cv 20 dict put}if_cv begin/bdf{bind def}bind def/isDeviceColor {/currentcolorspace where{pop currentcolorspace 0 get dup /DeviceGray e